{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AYDFMTJxgoFawkfQvSQUNF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is well-documented in `CLAUDE.md` and the frozen design docs. Here's a grounded summary of what it is:\n\n## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, no syncing). Markdown files are the source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **Ships as a persistent local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that runs as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`, binding `http://localhost:8777`, and renders the full dashboard HTML on every request while writing changes straight back to the markdown files.\n\n- **Core task/project manager.** It parses and edits markdown task files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`) to drive a task lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” with priorities, energy levels, due dates, notes, and per-domain views (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n\n- **A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`)** provides the same logic as command-line commands (`done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, `restore`, `dashboard`) and generates a static `dashboard.html` fallback.\n\n- **A self-test harness (`anchor_healthcheck.py`)** runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint and the R&D surfaces (v2/v3/v4, fully stubbed â€” never live `claude`), and writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Its major feature is an \"R&D control surface\"** â€” a per-project cockpit for running an AI agent \"trio\" (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Built up across four versions (v2 sessions/summaries/grass; v3 \"Mission Control\"; **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"**, now built and merged to master). It ships:\n  - real **ConPTY interactive terminals** (the one declared non-stdlib exception, optional `pywinpty`) with per-session **git-worktree isolation** and a durable session registry;\n  - **cached, grounding-validated session and project summaries** (generate-twice + hint-filter, through a stubbable runner seam);\n  - a **Paradigm-2 project window** â€” lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels (summary over a resizable xterm.js terminal), engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), grass idea board, deliverable launch-by-type, and cost/tokens/time rollups;\n  - **Ghost World Labs branding** (\"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\n- **Strict constraints by design:** Python 3.8+ stdlib only (one declared `pywinpty` exception for terminals, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan), all files plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool, single process owning port 8777 (`SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` guard).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: these claims are drawn from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked design-doc anchors, not re-verified against the current source this turn. If you want, I can spot-check specific claims (e.g., that v4 is actually wired into `render_project_window_html`) against the code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c1a6d46-ef3b-48b1-9915-905ee42cf830","uuid":"81c6c16d-40b3-4ce0-ac0c-16ec24aa1c56","request_id":"req_011Cc2MNCFJLon4n4iDKrLW5"}
